# rustkern/sessionid.rs - #745 session identity policy.
# Owner: proc/syscall.c (sys_session_lock), proc/users.c
# (users_create_first_admin) and main.c (the boot self-test).
#
# Two DECISIONS the non-root desktop flip turns on, kept out of the C plumbing
# that owns the mutable tables:
#   - may this session lock itself, given the lock reason, whether autologin is
#     active, and whether the session user can authenticate at all. The last
#     input is the one that makes an unlockable session impossible to create.
#   - which uid a human account gets: the first-boot admin (no longer 0) and
#     the next free uid for an account created later.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
