# rustkern/modex.rs - #740: Mode X (unchained 256-colour VGA). ONLY the thing no
# other video mode needs: what RESOLUTION the guest is in, derived from the CRTC
# because Mode X has no mode number to look it up by. Everything else (stride,
# start address, Line Compare, pan, Map Mask, Chain-4, Read Map Select) comes
# from dos_vga_decode_geom() in dosexec.c, which is the one decode every
# presenter shares.
# Callers: dos_present_modex(), dos_present_aspect() and the launch selftest,
# all in kernel/dos/dosexec.c.
dos_modex_geom_rs
dos_modex_selftest_rs

# rustkern/doscrtc.rs - #740: WHAT AN INT 10h MODE SET LEAVES IN THE CRTC, and
# the ONE definition of the CRTC-0x13 "unprogrammed" sentinel that decides the
# framebuffer row length. A real BIOS mode set writes all 25 CRTC registers;
# ours wrote a subset and inherited 0x0C/0x0D (start) and 0x13 (Offset) from
# whatever mode ran before, which are exactly the three whose ZERO value the
# decode reads as "use the mode default". Aladdin sets mode 0Dh then 13h, so
# the mode-0Dh Offset of 0x14 (40 bytes) survived and the chained presenter
# read the framebuffer at 40 bytes per row instead of 320 -> eight identical
# vertical columns.
# Callers: int10() mode-13h set and dos_vga_decode_geom(), both in
# kernel/dos/dosexec.c, plus the launch selftest.
dos_crtc_seed_mode13_rs
dos_crtc_stride_rs
dos_crtc_selftest_rs
drvmap_selftest_rs

