# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# rustkern/dragsess.rs - the cross-window drag session (Tier 5 "docking").
# NOT a strangler port: there is no C twin and no -DRUST_* flag, because there
# was never any C here. It is new kernel state whose whole risk surface is
# copying a Ring-3-sized byte range into and out of fixed buffers and indexing
# a fixed table by a Ring-3-supplied window handle, so it was written in Rust
# under the 2026-07-16 Rust-by-default rule. Called from proc/syscall.c
# (SYS_DRAG_*), gui/window.c has NO hook, and main.c runs the boot self-test.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
